# Cursor execution adapter

This file applies only when Cursor is the selected client. It does not set a universal model or agent count. Root [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) owns permissions, Git, quality and implementation/acceptance split. Read selected CHANGE.md, TASKS dispatch index and [parent policy](../../.agents/references/bounded-parent-orchestration.md), not all planner files.

**Commission:** one Change and one preferred measurable outcome. Seven actual tasks, including nested assignments, is a strong default. Target 5–10 minutes of active implementation. [Submission standard](../../.agents/references/planning-artifact-quality.md) and [severity](../../AGENTS.md#finding-severity-and-blocking). Return a newly commissioned packet that is incoherent, unsafe or forces architectural invention, and name the exact gap. A count or size signal alone is not that return. No autonomous split, replan or auto-next. An already commissioned batch proceeds through its tasks without another owner confirmation at each routine checkpoint.

**Branch guard:** dedicated Change branch and linked worktree; never switch the primary checkout. A Design's Changes use the recorded `implementation/<design-slug>` branch, or its grandfathered ref, and do not join main. Run `node scripts/repo-tools/change-branch-guard.mjs --change <ID> --target <reference-branch>` there before edits, with `--design` and `--grandfather` when the packet names them.

**Parent:** Composer 2.5 Standard, per [.cursor/MODEL-POLICY.md](../MODEL-POLICY.md). Dispatch one substantive task to the Composer implementer; up to two children only for proven independent waves. Tiny obvious mechanical edits may be direct. Continue the commissioned lifecycle across internal checkpoints, including the Change-level join and clean retirement, with no repeated approval. Shared-checkout children do not stage or commit. The parent verifies the assigned checks and the diff, archives the completed packet, commits, and joins through `scripts/repo-tools/change-lifecycle.mjs` when the Change-level gate passes. A construction gate may be source inspection plus the named downstream proof owner. The join is not complete while the open packet remains on the implementation target. Indispensable Change-level acceptance still stops at IMPLEMENTED — ACCEPTANCE PENDING and keeps the worktree. Design-level acceptance that the Design left pending does not. Heavy joint acceptance stays with the acceptance lead and owner. [Delegation policy](../../.agents/references/bounded-parent-orchestration.md#0a-budget-first-composer-dispatcher-contract-2026-11-21).

**Child:** one T-ID and direct source/test/contract anchors, decided edit, only the checks that card assigns, concise receipt. A construction card may assign no executable check. PATCH/VERIFY or precisely bounded factual investigation; no architecture survey, test campaign, swarms, paid escalation, unrelated refactors or full suite per child. Local mechanical debugging allowed for an unexpected defect; do not chase a failure the packet already expected. Report the exact contradiction and reproducer.

**Resources:** [owned dev runbook](../../docs/runbooks/dev-worktree-stacks.md); source-only first, no speculative stacks or bypass. Park only own attempted workloads, preserve data/reservations. No paid calls, protected mutation or destruction without explicit authority.

**Resume:** recover current Change/T-ID/receipts, recheck HEAD, worktree, scope, resources and proof. Do not redo finished investigation or trust summary as proof. Report edits, tests/negative, blockers and measured spend if available. [Code quality](../../.agents/rules/code-quality.md).
